From 24520824dc27405ccfae3e097f34b5d1e7235be4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: woahwhattheheck <293286387+woahwhattheheck@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 00:36:24 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Retry kept server fallbacks like other suspended boundaries

Follow-ups for keeping the server fallback of a browser-only boundary while
its client render is suspended:

- Retry at a normal retry lane once the content is unblocked, instead of the
  dehydrated state's OffscreenLane, so the content doesn't wait behind an
  unrelated suspended transition.
- Honor ScheduleRetry when completing a kept boundary, like any boundary
  showing its fallback, so skipped siblings are prerendered and content that
  suspends the commit on a stylesheet is retried.
- Don't keep the server fallback if the props, legacy context or a context it
  could read changed, and retry a kept boundary when a parent context
  changes, like a client rendered boundary showing its fallback.
- Don't keep the server fallback if the content spawned a deferred render
  (useDeferredValue); only the regular fallback path schedules it.
- Clear the ChildDeletion flag left over from the client render attempt
  instead of searching a deletion list that unwinding already dropped.
- Suppress the invalid-compare Flow error for renderers without hydration,
  like the same comparison in the first pass.
- Use LF line endings in the touched files, like the rest of the repo.
- Move the regression tests next to the other browser() tests in
  ReactDOMFizzServer-test.
